An async function is declared with the `async` keyword and automatically returns a Promise. The `await` keyword pauses execution inside async functions until a Promise resolves.

```typescript
async function fetchUser(id: number): Promise<User> {
  const user = await db.getUser(id);
  return user;
}
```

Define an interface for your props:

```typescript
interface ButtonProps {
  label: string;
  onClick: () => void;
  disabled?: boolean;
}

const Button: React.FC<ButtonProps> = ({ label, onClick, disabled }) => (
  <button onClick={onClick} disabled={disabled}>{label}</button>
);
```

Parse the value to number:

```typescript
// Before
const age: number = '25'; // Error!

// After
const age: number = parseInt('25', 10);
// or use unary plus: const age = +'25';
```

Both define shapes. interface supports declaration merging and extension. type supports unions, intersections, and tuples.

```typescript
interface User { id: number; name: string; }
interface Admin extends User { role: 'admin'; }

type Status = 'ok' | 'error'; // only type can do this
type AdminUser = User & { role: 'admin' };
```
Rule: interface for objects, type for everything else.

